begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(2)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}4\\sqrt{2}{sin}^{3/2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sin}^{3/2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta $ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sin}^{3/2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =8\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}}{5}({(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5/2}-{0}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{5}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385214 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385215 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385216 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385217 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385218 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1041 "selection" 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385215 13194139536132 true] [17592186385213 1110